        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "caf7ea23-4c85-5b7a-9857-6b648db0f2f8",
        "text": "This chunk describes Karakoram mountains and their elevations.\n\nThis chunk is about:\n- Places: Gilgit-Baltistan\n- Mountain ranges: Karakoram, Hispar Muztagh, Yengisogat\n- Mountains: Distaghil Sar, The Crown\n\nFacts:\n- Distaghil Sar is the highest mountain in the Hispar Muztagh, which is a subrange of the Karakoram mountain range in Gilgit-Baltistan.\n- Distaghil Sar has an approximately 3 km-long summit ridge above 7400 m with three distinct summits: the northwest summit at 7885 m, the central summit at 7760 m, and the southeast summit at 7696 m or 7535 m.\n- The Crown has an elevation of 7295 m and is the highest peak in the Yengisogat subrange of the Karakoram.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ff3fdc71-756c-58e8-b37b-c74e0656e337",
        "text": "Page: Distaghil Sar. Sentence: Disteghil Sar or Distaghil Sar (Urdu: ‎ ) is the highest mountain in the Hispar Muztagh, a subrange of the Karakoram mountain range, in Gilgit-Baltistan.\nPage: Distaghil Sar. Sentence: The mountain has an about 3 km long top ridge above 7400m with three distinct summits: (north)west 7885m, central 7760 m, and (south)east 7696m or 7535m ().\nPage: The Crown (mountain). Sentence: Its summit has an elevation of 7295 m and it is the highest peak in the Yengisogat subrange of the Karakoram.",
